    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">Dear colleague,</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">We are pleased to invite you to our next webinar: <strong>The Intelligence Edge: How Electoral Bodies Can Monitor and Manage the Information Environment</strong>, taking place on <strong>Thursday, 4 June 2026 at 14:00&ndash;15:00 UTC (15:00&ndash;16:00 BST)</strong>.</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">Election Management Bodies (EMBs) operate in an increasingly complex information environment &mdash; tracking legislative changes, monitoring media coverage, identifying mis- and disinformation, and responding to a 24/7 news cycle. The demands on institutions to act quickly, accurately, and with authority have never been greater.</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 24px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">This webinar explores how EMBs can build structured intelligence-gathering and monitoring practices to strengthen decision-making, improve resilience, and support more effective public communication.</p>

